---
import { Heading, Markdown } from '@splendidlabz/astro'
import { Code } from 'astro-expressive-code/components'
---

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="vertical items-center gap-4">
      <Heading class="gap-4 mb-2" center>
        <h2 class="h2 max-w-[16em] text-zorange-500">
          <Markdown inline>
            One More Example: Changing Colours On Hover And Focus States ---
            Without the HTML bloat
          </Markdown>
        </h2>

        <p class="h2-subhead max-w-[38rem]">
          <Markdown inline>
            Simply by using our in-house pigment utility
          </Markdown>
        </p>
      </Heading>

      <div class="vertical gap-10 w-full max-w-[46rem] mx-auto">
        <div class="grid-simple bp8:[--cols:2] items-center">
          <div class="prose-responsive">
            <!-- prettier-ignore -->
            <Markdown>
              Now say you wanna create a few buttons with different colours. This should be basic, simple stuff. 
            </Markdown>
          </div>

          <div class="bp8:-order-1 vertical items-center gap-3 card">
            <button class="button pigment-orange-filled">
              Pigment Orange Filled
            </button>
            <button class="button pigment-orange-outline">
              Pigment Orange Outline
            </button>
            <button class="button pigment-purple-outline">
              Pigment Purple Outline
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- With Tailwind only -->
        <div class="vertical gap-3">
          <h3 class="h4 text-zorange-500">With Tailwind only</h3>
          <div class="prose-responsive">
            <!-- prettier-ignore -->
            <Markdown>
              There's lots of code to write here --- the layout classes, the base colours, and even colours for hover and focus states. Just look at the bloat! 
            </Markdown>
          </div>
          <div class="card card-divided-vertical p-0 !bg-zpurple-1000s">
            <header class="horizontal items-baseline px-3 py-2">
              <span>HTML</span>
            </header>
            <div class="code-comparison">
              <Code
                code={`<button class="flex items-center justify-center px-[1.25em] py-[0.5em] text-xl leading-[21px] rounded-xl border-2 border-zorange-500 text-zorange-500 hover:bg-zorange-800 hover:text-white focus:bg-zorange-800 focus:text-white">Orange Outline</button>`}
                lang="html"
                wrap
              />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- With Tailwind and CSS -->
        <div class="vertical gap-3">
          <h3 class="h4 text-zorange-500">With both Tailwind and CSS</h3>
          <div class="prose-responsive">
            <!-- prettier-ignore -->
            <Markdown>
              I'll cheat a little by showing you my actual `pigment` system.  where I've written all the classes needed beforehand, so we only need to change the background, text, and border colours on each state. 
            </Markdown>
          </div>
          <div class="card card-divided-vertical p-0 !bg-zpurple-1000s">
            <header class="horizontal items-baseline px-3 py-2">
              <span>HTML</span>
            </header>
            <div class="code-comparison">
              <Code
                code={`<button class="button pigment-orange-outline">Orange Outline</button>`}
                lang="html"
                wrap
              />
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="card card-divided-vertical p-0 !bg-zpurple-1000s">
            <header class="horizontal items-baseline px-3 py-2">
              <span>CSS</span>
            </header>
            <div class="code-comparison">
              <Code
                code={`/* button and pigment defined and reused in every project */

@utility pigment-orange-outline {
  --bg-color: transparent;
  --bg-hover-color: var(--color-zorange-800);
  --text-color: var(--color-zorange-500);
  --text-hover-color: #fff;
  --border-color: var(--color-zorange-500);
}`}
                lang="css"
                wrap
              />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
